CNN ROCK PAPER SCISSORS — WINDOWS QUICK START
================================================

This is a playable webcam game. It uses a small CNN trained on your own real webcam images.
You need Python 3.10 or 3.11 recommended, a webcam, and an internet connection for installation.

1) Extract this ZIP into a folder.
2) Open Command Prompt in that folder.
3) Create a virtual environment (recommended):
   py -3.11 -m venv .venv
   .venv\Scripts\activate

4) Install packages:
   python -m pip install --upgrade pip
   pip install tensorflow opencv-python pygame numpy

5) Collect your own images:
   python collect_data.py
   Hold your hand in the center green square.
   Press R when showing Rock, P for Paper, S for Scissors.
   Collect 100-200 or more images for EACH class. Vary lighting, distance, and hand position.
   Press Q to quit.
   Images are saved into dataset/rock, dataset/paper, dataset/scissors.

6) Train the CNN:
   python train_model.py
   Training creates rps_cnn.keras.

7) Play:
   python game.py
   Show one gesture inside the green square and press SPACE to play a round.
   Press ESC to exit.

IMPORTANT
- The model is not included because it must be trained on your collected images.
- CNN accuracy depends on the quality and variety of your own collected images.
- Keep the same webcam, crop area, and general lighting while collecting and playing.
- If the camera cannot open, close Zoom/Teams/Camera and try again.
- TensorFlow installation support depends on your Python version and system. Python 3.10/3.11 on 64-bit Windows is a practical starting point.
- This is a starter project. It may need tuning if your hand/background changes significantly.
